{
  "info": {
    "name": "CrushSVG API",
    "_postman_id": "9f2c7e3a-1b4d-4e6f-8a9c-0d1e2f3a4b5c",
    "description": "# CrushSVG API\n\nConvert SVG to pixel-perfect PNG from any application.\n\n## Quickstart\n\n1. Import this collection and the **CrushSVG API - Production** environment.\n2. Set `email` and `password` in the environment (or use the collection defaults).\n3. Run **Authentication → Register** to create an account (then verify the email from your inbox).\n4. Run **Authentication → Login** — the `accessToken` is stored automatically for all protected requests.\n5. Try **Conversion → Convert to PNG (JSON)** with the sample SVG.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Guests get **3 free conversions per 10 minutes** (no login needed).\n- Signed-in users are unlimited.\n- Access tokens expire after 15 minutes — run **Authentication → Refresh Token** to get a new pair (the refresh cookie must be present in a browser context; from Postman, copy `refreshToken` into the `crushsvg_refresh` cookie manually if needed).\n- Full reference: https://crush-svg.vercel.app/api-docs",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://crush-svg.vercel.app",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "demo@example.com",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "super-secret-123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "resetToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "verifyToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sampleSvg",
      "value": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"><circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"50\" r=\"40\" fill=\"#D94A1E\"/></svg>",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Authentication",
      "description": "Create an account, sign in, and manage sessions. Protected endpoints use a Bearer access token (set automatically by Login).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Jane Doe\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Registers a new user and sends a verification email. The account must be verified before login. If the email already belongs to a Google/GitHub-only account, the password is linked to it instead of failing.\n\nRate limit: 3 / min per IP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Registers successfully', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(201);",
                  "  pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Sends verification email', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(json.payload.message).to.include('verify');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"rememberMe\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Authenticates and returns a token pair. The access token is saved to the `accessToken` collection variable so all protected requests work automatically.\n\nRate limit: 10 / min per IP. Brute-force protection: 429 `account_locked` after repeated failures."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Logs in successfully', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "});",
                  "if (json.success && json.payload && json.payload.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.payload.token.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.payload.token.refreshToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', json.payload.sessionId);",
                  "  pm.test('Tokens stored', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')).to.not.eql('');",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes the current session and clears the refresh cookie. Returns 200 even without a token, so clients can always treat it as success."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Logs out successfully', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(json.payload.message).to.include('Logged out');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout All Devices",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout-all",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "logout-all"]
            },
            "description": "Revokes every active session for the current user."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Revokes all sessions', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().payload.message).to.include('all devices');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Exchanges the refresh token (crushsvg_refresh cookie) for a fresh pair and stores the new access token. From Postman the cookie is sent by a browser context only — for a full manual flow, copy `refreshToken` from the Login response into the `crushsvg_refresh` cookie (Domain: your host, Path: /).\n\nRate limit: 120 / min per IP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.success && json.payload && json.payload.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.payload.token.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.payload.token.refreshToken);",
                  "  pm.test('Refreshed token stored', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')).to.not.eql('');",
                  "  });",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('Session is dead (token_missing / token_invalid)', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.success).to.eql(false);",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Change Password",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/change-password",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "change-password"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"currentPassword\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"even-more-secret-456\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Changes the account password and signs the user out of every device. Requires a fresh login afterwards.\n\nRate limit: 5 / min per IP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Changes password', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().payload.message).to.include('Password changed');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "OAuth Sign In (Google)",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/oauth/google",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "oauth", "google"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"firebaseToken\": \"<firebase-id-token>\",\n  \"rememberMe\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Signs in with a Firebase ID token. The provider path segment must match the token's signing provider: google, github, or x. The access token is saved to the `accessToken` variable automatically.\n\nRate limit: 10 / min per IP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.success && json.payload && json.payload.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.payload.token.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.payload.token.refreshToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', json.payload.sessionId);",
                  "}",
                  "pm.test('Responds', () => { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 400, 401, 404]); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Passwords & Email Verification",
      "description": "Account recovery and email verification. Token links expire after 30 minutes (password reset) or 24 hours (email verification).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Forgot Password",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/passwords/forgot",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "passwords", "forgot"]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Sends a reset link if the account exists. The response is identical either way (anti-enumeration). Works for social-only accounts too.\n\nRate limit: 3 / min per IP."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Accepts the request', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "});"
